{
  "name": "Image time layer",
  "description": "A picture's fetched-at time as an `imageTime` layer instead of the image's own `timestamp` keys. The camera layer carries no timestamp keys, so it draws no chip of its own (`showTimestamp` false). The first time layer sits above the image in the layer list and links to it; the second links to it too; the third links to a layer the document does not have. The chip's text size comes from the layer's frame when drawn, so nothing resolved carries a size. A fixture carries no picture bytes, so every layer resolves with no fetched-at time (`fetchedAt` absent) and draws nothing here: what both sides pin is the link and the element base. An `imageTime` alone asks for no picture, so the fetch list is the image's own camera once.",
